yoyo find now refuses extra arguments with exit 2 instead of silently folding them into the pattern. A single argument containing a space now reaches the search as-is, with no literal quotes added. It's committed as d6adc484 and goes out with this session's push. Formatting, clippy, build and the full test suite all pass.

I ran the recorded commands with the built binary before and after the change. The "before" readings matched the assessment on all four:

| command | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| find main src (in this repo) | No files matching 'main src'., exit 0 | error on stderr naming 'main' 'src' and showing how to quote a spaced name, exit 2 |
| find zz9 /nonexistent_dir | false "no files" message, exit 0 | same error, exit 2 |
| find "a b" (with dir sp/a b.rs present) | No files matching '"a b"'., exit 0 | finds dir sp/a b.rs, exit 0 |
| bare find | usage, exit 0 | same usage text, exit 2 |
| find main, and a search with no match | exit 0 | unchanged |

What changed:
• **src/dispatch_sub.rs:** the `find` arm no longer uses `quote_args_as_command`. A new helper, `find_pattern_from_argv`, passes one argument through unchanged, refuses two or more, and treats no arguments as "show usage".
• **`src/commands_search.rs:** bare usage now returns exit 2, the same way bare grep` does.
• **Where I departed from the plan:** it said the helper's error for zero arguments should carry the usage text. I left the usage text in the handler instead, so there is only one copy of it. The interactive /find throws away the exit code, so it behaves exactly as before.
• Tests:
  • A table test of the helper (0, 1, a spaced argument, an argument with an embedded ", 2 and 3 arguments).
  • A check that a single plain argument comes back unchanged.
  • A check that control characters in arguments are escaped in the error.
  • An end-to-end test in tests/integration.rs, find_refuses_extra_args_and_passes_one_spaced_arg_verbatim.
• **Test check:** I disabled the two-or-more branch (marked `NEUTERED`) and re-ran, all in one command. The two unit tests and the end-to-end test failed by name and the plain-argument check stayed green. After restoring, everything passed and no marker was left.
• **ARCHITECTURE.md:** a short note on the change.

One oddity: my first edit adding the helper reported success but wasn't in the file. I added it again and checked with grep before building.

Not done (also listed in the commit message): a real path argument for /find, the other #1009 commands, the interactive /find, and no-match results (still exit 0 by design).

I posted a before/after comment on #1009 and on #982, and gh issue view 1009 --comments shows it. Both comments list what's still left. For #1009, nine other commands still go through quote_args_as_command. For #982, I re-ran bare blame, run and docs today and they still exit 0.
